  },
  {
    "rec_key": "3805460:b9fc49b0e3",
    "primary_label": "explicit_instructional_time",
    "flags_json": "[\"duplicate\"]",
    "note": "See also www.dunseith.k12.nd.us/o/dps/page/2025-2026-school-year-calendar\n\nThis is really subtle. This is primarily an academic calendar. However,  the calendar image that appears to be embedded in the page, there is a block at the bottom center that starts with an underlined \"Days of Classroom Instruction -147\" In that block is an explicit statement of instructional *hours*. It's shows up in .txt, tesseract_raster, and tesseract_screenshot.\n\n---\nDays of Classroom Instruction \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026..147\n\nHigh School Days 147 x 7.5 hrs. per day = 1102.5 hrs.\nState Requirement = 1,050 hrs.\nElementary Days 147 x 7.25 hrs. per day= 1065.75 hrs.\nState Requirement = 963.5 hrs.\n---\nThis shows that each High school day is 7.5 hours and each elementary school day is 7.25 hours. From this, we should be able to derive that each high school day is 450 minutes and each elementary school day is 435 minutes. I'm unclear whether North Dakota or Dunseith Public School District 4M groups middle school with the elementary schools or the high schools (as middle school is typically categorized with high school as a secondary school).\n\nWe'll need to keep an eye out for academic calendars that have information like this so we don't prematurely filter them out when there's a gold nugget buried in there.\n\n\n",
    "status": "labeled",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-25T00:37:28Z"
  },
